     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the usual maximum for adults. The maximum is 3,200 mg/day under physician supervision, and outpatient OTC labeling caps it at 1,200 mg/day. A dose that high carries a serious risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day)\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **1600 mg/day total**, divided into a different schedule\n\nIf 1600 mg four times daily is what you want, please confirm that explicitly. If you'd like, I can add a note with the clinical rationale. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and frequency and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
